// Owned-string rvalue TEMPORARY in a loop condition — one heap buffer is allocated per
// iteration by `seed.concat(...)` and must RAII-drop each pass (per-iteration drop slot in the
// loop-and-a-half rewrite). A missing drop leaks once per iteration (ASan catches it); the loop
// is counter-bounded so it terminates, and the owned temp is re-evaluated every pass.
fn int32 main()
{
    string seed = "xy";
    int32 r = 0;

    // while: the concat temp (heap-owned, length 4 > 0 always) is created + freed each iteration;
    // `i < 3` bounds the loop to 3 passes.
    int32 i = 0;
    while (seed.concat(other: seed).length() > 0 && i < 3) { r = r + 1; i = i + 1; }

    // for: same, iter clause advances k; 4 passes.
    for (int32 k = 0; seed.concat(other: seed).length() > 0 && k < 4; k = k + 1) { r = r + 10; }

    return r;   // 3 + 40 = 43
}
